35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: The neighbouring block’s charge left three households in arrears, and two stopped attending meetings.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: I watched two mornings. Eleven bikes left between seven and nine, and four times someone had to move another first.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"- **May**: The ledger shows capital work needs a levy, and the station park charges 2,600 yen with fourteen households waiting.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,George,,"- **George**: The handover file shows three hours monthly just for current collections, and the display frame needs greasing twice a year.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: The sticker register shows some flats have three bikes, and daily riders said they’d rather pay than be counted equally.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: And the complaint log had nine notes about leaning bikes, all ignored because no one was responsible.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: The row under the eaves stays dry, but past the downpipe, a saddle is still wet the next morning.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"- **May**: So we’d be competing with a 2,600 yen option that fourteen people are already waiting for.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,George,,- **George**: Three hours monthly is already a burden. Adding per-place billing on top of that would be impossible for one person.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: The minutes show the same flats held the covered spots for five years, with no review recorded.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,- **Misaki**: That silence in the logs explains why things got so tense. We need a clear owner for the rules.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,- **Shizue**: That wet saddle detail is why I’m worried. We can’t just leave bikes in the rain and expect them to stay in good shape.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"- **May**: @George, if billing is that heavy, maybe we shouldn’t charge at all. What’s the alternative?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,George,,"@May, I’m not against charging, but I am against one person drowning in paperwork. We need a system that doesn’t rely on a single hero.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@May, the riders said they’d pay to avoid equal counting. Maybe that’s the key to a fairer system.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, but if we charge, we risk the same arrears and silence the neighbours suffered. We need a system that doesn’t punish people for missing a payment.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with Misaki. We must avoid that coldness. Perhaps we focus on the physical layout first, like the dry spots, to ease the morning rush.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"@Shizue, layout helps, but it doesn’t solve the money question. If we don’t charge, who pays for the repairs?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,George,,"@May, the ledger says capital work needs a levy. We could charge a flat fee for maintenance, not per space.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@George, a flat fee sounds fair, but the minutes show the same flats kept the best spots for years. How do we fix that bias?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
